    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-gray-900 tracking-tight mb-3">
      Why You Must Air-Seal Attic Top Plates Before Blown-In Insulation
    </h1>
    <p class="text-base text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-6">
      Adding 16 inches of fresh blown cellulose or fiberglass over an unsealed attic floor is one of the most common energy upgrade mistakes. Here is why thermal insulation without air sealing fails, and the exact step-by-step protocol for sealing drywall top plates and plumbing chases.
    </p>

    <!-- Quick Stats Grid -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 pt-6 border-t border-gray-100">
      <div>
        <div class="text-xs text-gray-500">Air Infiltration Loss</div>
